[SPEAKER_01]: Can you regard it as yours?

1003
01:01:09,233 --> 01:01:09,833
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't want it.

1004
01:01:11,374 --> 01:01:11,614
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

1005
01:01:12,375 --> 01:01:15,076
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you regard it as yours, if it's seen as painful?

1006
01:01:15,876 --> 01:01:16,117
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

1007
01:01:16,677 --> 01:01:20,019
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you regard it as yours, if it's seen as constantly oppressing you?

1008
01:01:20,519 --> 01:01:20,999
[SPEAKER_00]: Not at all.

1009
01:01:21,199 --> 01:01:22,640
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

1010
01:01:22,660 --> 01:01:26,802
[SPEAKER_01]: So, not seeing it, in such and such, in all these manners, that's why you regard it as yours.

1011
01:01:27,702 --> 01:01:29,964
[SPEAKER_01]: You start seeing it, you can't regard it as yours.

1012
01:01:31,785 --> 01:01:33,605
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you don't need to then choose the escape.

1013
01:01:33,826 --> 01:01:34,906
[SPEAKER_01]: The escape is automatic.

1014
01:01:35,967 --> 01:01:38,448
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding anicca correctly, understanding dukkha correctly,

1015
01:01:38,881 --> 01:01:40,303
[SPEAKER_01]: Anatta is automatic.

1016
01:01:41,886 --> 01:01:43,468
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the necessary result of it.

1017
01:01:44,810 --> 01:01:46,533
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not, oh, now I do the anatta.

1018
01:01:46,633 --> 01:01:47,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Now I do the anatta.

